    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "035fcf25_b38f9b5d",
        "filename": "drivers/usb/gadget/configfs_uevent.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-23T00:47:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that this is ugly, but sending a single uevent would require userspace changes as well. We are attempting to cleanup these drivers without changes to userspace as we don\u0027t want to be supporting multiple revisions going forward.",
      "parentUuid": "12d76bb8_cbf5ccc6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "2ae2b5e0f8cd2772b3efd256361728da7ecb57f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d44706e9_eabcc410",
        "filename": "drivers/usb/gadget/configfs_uevent.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T16:44:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, a single `KOBJ_CHANGE` event happens, userspace wakes up, reads the sysfs file, and then does something with it.  You aren\u0027t allowed to send a bunch of them all at once, that\u0027s abusing the api in bad ways (and making the system slower.)",
      "parentUuid": "035fcf25_b38f9b5d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "2ae2b5e0f8cd2772b3efd256361728da7ecb57f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
